## Architecture Issues

### 7. **Monolithic Structure**

The entire codebase is in one IIFE with 2000+ lines. This makes it:
- Hard to test
- Difficult to maintain
- Impossible to reuse components

**Fix**: Modularize into classes/modules
```javascript
class DOMInspector {
  constructor() {
    this.state = new StateManager();
    this.ui = new UIManager();
    this.overlay = new OverlayManager();
    this.responsive = new ResponsiveManager();
  }
}

class StateManager {
  constructor() {
    this.current = STATES.IDLE;
    this.listeners = new Set();
  }
  
  setState(newState) { /* ... */ }
  subscribe(callback) { /* ... */ }
}

class UIManager {
  createButton() { /* ... */ }
  createPanel() { /* ... */ }
}
```

### 8. **Tight Coupling**

Functions directly access and modify global state `S` everywhere.

**Fix**: Use dependency injection
```javascript
class EventHandler {
  constructor(state, ui, overlay) {
    this.state = state;
    this.ui = ui;
    this.overlay = overlay;
  }
  
  handleMouseMove(e) {
    const element = this.getTargetElement(e);
    this.overlay.highlight(element);
  }
}
```

